# Annex A.3 - `yBarSolverFromLambda`

**Location:** inside `GaussianTwoFactors.m`, inside `methods`.

```matlab
function yBar = yBarSolverFromLambda(obj, lambda, By, args)
    % Solves for yBar(x):
    %
    %     1 = sum_i lambda_i(x) * exp(-By_i * yBar)

    arguments
        obj (1,1) GaussianTwoFactors;
        lambda (:,1) double;
        By (:,1) double;
        args.ySeed (1,1) double = 0;
        args.maxExpansion (1,1) double = 30;
        args.tolerance (1,1) double = 1e-10;
    end

    lambda = lambda(:);
    By = By(:);

    scalarF = @(y) obj.getYBarValue(y, lambda, By);

    yLow = args.ySeed - 0.01;
    yHigh = args.ySeed + 0.01;

    fLow = scalarF(yLow);
    fHigh = scalarF(yHigh);

    expansion = 0;

    while fLow * fHigh > 0 && expansion < args.maxExpansion
        width = yHigh - yLow;

        yLow = yLow - 2 * width;
        yHigh = yHigh + 2 * width;

        fLow = scalarF(yLow);
        fHigh = scalarF(yHigh);

        expansion = expansion + 1;
    end

    if fLow * fHigh > 0
        yBar = NaN;
        return;
    end

    yBar = fzero(scalarF, [yLow, yHigh]);

    residual = scalarF(yBar);

    if ~isfinite(yBar) || abs(residual) > args.tolerance
        yBar = NaN;
    end
end
```

